    [Ops][Misc] Refactor patches to separate V1-only patches and flatten V2/shared patches (#19957)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    This PR refactors the worker patch structure in `vllm_ascend`. It
    separates Model Runner V1-only (MRv1) patches into a dedicated
    `patch_v1` package (e.g., `vllm_ascend/patch/worker/patch_v1/`) and
    flattens V2/shared patches directly into `vllm_ascend/patch/worker/`
    (removing the `patch_v2` subdirectory). This reorganization isolates
    V1-specific code, making it easier to drop V1 support in the future.
    Documentation, tests, and imports across the codebase have been updated
    to reflect these new paths.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No. This is a code refactoring and reorganization of internal patches.
    
    ### How was this patch tested？
    Existing unit tests and end-to-end tests have been updated with the
    corrected import paths and should pass to verify that functionality is
    preserved.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: I reviewed whether this change
    involves
    boundary conditions (e.g. empty input, single/zero element, min/max
    values,
    off-by-one, sequence-length limits, integer overflow). Where applicable,
    I
    added unit tests covering these edge cases in `tests/ut/` or
    `tests/e2e/`.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: If this PR fixes a bug, I added a regression
    test
      that would fail without the fix.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage**: I covered abnormal paths
    (exceptions,
    timeouts, out-of-range, division by zero) in addition to the happy path.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: New tests assert real behavior
    and are
      not written merely to satisfy CI.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: If this PR touches a performance-sensitive
    path,
      I attached benchmark results and added performance regression tests.
    
    
